   "output": "Read only the page below. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse. Answer each question from the page alone. When the page does not say, answer \"Not stated\".\n\n<<<PAGE\n# term-weave\n\n## What it does\n\n`term-weave` drafts a glossary of project terms from documents in a folder you supply. Every drafted definition links to the passage that supports it.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse it when project vocabulary is scattered across documents or newcomers encounter unexplained terms.\n\n## How it works\n\nRun the skill manually:\n\n```text\n/term-weave <source-folder>\n```\n\nIt reads Markdown and plain-text documents and ignores other file types. It never changes the source documents.\n\nIf the folder is missing or contains no readable supported documents, it stops and explains the problem without drafting.\n\n## What you get\n\nThe skill writes `GLOSSARY.md` in the working directory, with entries sorted alphabetically.\n\nIt does not invent definitions. Terms without a supporting explanation appear under **Unresolved terms**, after the defined entries.\n\nIf sources give conflicting definitions, the skill preserves both in one entry, links each source, and marks the entry **Conflict**.\nPAGE>>>\n\nQuestions:\n(a) Will term-weave change the source documents?\n(b) How do you run it?\n(c) What happens when two sources define the same term differently?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"a\": \"...\", \"b\": \"...\", \"c\": \"...\"}. Start the answer to (a) with Yes, No, or Not stated.",
